"answer": "Project Zenith is a high-priority initiative aimed at driving innovation, optimizing cloud storage, and enhancing data analytics and visualization. Key milestones include a $2M budget approval, a $500k allocation for Phase One, and a $55k increase for the compliance plan. The project involves multiple phases: Phase One kicked off in June/July 2023 with Sarah Tan and Marcus Cole as leads; Phase Two achieved a breakthrough in predictive analytics by November. Recent updates include a security protocol update effective January, a call for R&D ideas by July 20th, and a celebration of the testing phase completion on October 10th. Feedback is being sought by the end of November, and a detailed report will be shared on November 20th."
